    {
      "kind": "client",
      "evidence": "Global.Text 42062 'Robgoblin Adept Trouble!' (title), 42057 (card), objective 42063; icon 4541."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reference",
      "evidence": "Starter: reference Npcs.json Id 3565 drawn at [-1593.01, -28.14, 662.44] (npc_spawns_extra.json spawn_guid 100000003565, FreeRealms-Legacy FabledRealms.lua). Region The Wilds, place The Wilds."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reference",
      "evidence": "BJX fork Resources/Battles.json Id 43 ('Robgoblin Adept Trouble! (the live random encounter: a robgoblin adept and her friends)'): scene sg_random_encounter_02, entry, exit, 3 waves, 10 spawns ({'Robgoblin Wiz-ord': 5, 'Robgoblin Knuckle Head': 4, 'Robgoblin Adept': 1})."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) Every spot inside the scene is the fork's generated layout, not an original one. Zone number 1242 is the fork's; ours must be assigned and the scene sg_random_encounter_02 has not been loaded by our server yet (the eleven shipped battles all use sg_random_encounter_clearing). Triggers: at-start spawns are actors, later waves follow the one before (the fork's 1.5 s delay is dropped). Knockouts and score are the design's defaults; coins and XP are the shipped battles' values, not the fork's 30 coins / 140 stars."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) Not proven in the client: this scene needs one native load, and the starter or door of `entry` is drawn by the entrances work, not by this file. Each kind's rank here decides its health and hit at the fight's tier."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) rc-0137 prize wheel (2026-11-12): 'Robgoblin Adept Trouble!' has no wheel of its own on the wiki; the wiki's item pages put its prize wheel with 'Arachnia's Lair' (Ninja's Blade of Shuriken Storm; Warrior’s Axe of Earthquake; Wizard's Wand of Firestorm; Medic's Scalpel of Alarm), so it spins that wheel, from fandom 'Arachnia's Lair' (revision 49334), one per combat job, and 99 coins. The same pages also name Highroad Hijinx, Petty Yetis!, Robgoblin Creek!, arachnia_s_lair."
    }
  ]
